+## Core Submission & Storage
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit with a base revision ID, the system SHALL store the submission with visit ID, base revision ID, author ID, idempotency key, complete payload, and server receipt timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload and base revision ID, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
+- [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload or base revision ID, the system SHALL reject the submission with a conflict error and leave the original submission unchanged.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same base revision ID are accepted from different authors, the system SHALL preserve all original submissions as competing revisions of the same visit.
+- [ ] **REC-005**: A submission with a null base revision ID is the visit's initial creation and SHALL not conflict with other competing revisions.
+
+## Current State & Resolution Status
+
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a visit has exactly one revision, that revision SHALL be designated as current; retrieval SHALL return that revision's complete payload and mark the visit as resolved.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a visit has two or more competing revisions (multiple submissions with the same base revision ID), the visit SHALL be marked as unresolved; retrieval SHALL return the list of competing revisions without designating a current state.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a coordinator selects one competing revision as current, the system SHALL designate that revision as current, archive the unselected revisions, and mark the visit as resolved.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a coordinator submits a manual resolution by citing two or more competing revisions as predecessors, that submission SHALL become the current revision and the original competing revisions SHALL be marked as resolved-by-merge.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When retrieving a visit's state, the system SHALL include metadata for each revision: author ID, base revision ID, and server receipt timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: A visit is export-eligible only when it has a current resolved revision.
+
+## Resolution Operations
+
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When a coordinator selects a competing revision as current, the system SHALL record the coordinator's identity, the list of competing submission IDs, the selection outcome, and the resolution timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When a coordinator manually merges competing revisions, the system SHALL accept a new submission that names the competing revision IDs as predecessors and SHALL treat it as the resolving revision.
+- [ ] **REC-022**: Resolution operations (selection or manual merge) are immutable; a resolved visit cannot be re-opened for re-review.
